Subject: [PATCH 2/2] scaled_mm: do not select the DeepGEMM FP8 kernel on sm_120

DeepGEMM has no sm_120 scale-factor layout, so selecting this kernel makes
weight loading die in process_weights_after_loading:

  transform_sf_into_required_layout ->
  Assertion error (deepgemm-src/csrc/apis/layout.hpp:60):
  Unknown SF transformation

is_deep_gemm_supported() only checks the env flag, import success and
"Hopper or Blackwell", and sm_120 passes that while lacking the kernels.
Declining selection here lets the framework fall back to another
Fp8BlockScaledMMLinearKernel rather than crash.

Scoped to this kernel deliberately: DeepGEMM's MoE path (DEEPGEMM_MXFP4)
does work on sm_120 and is the hot path for a 256-expert model, so the
global VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM switch is the wrong instrument.

--- a/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/deep_gemm.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/scaled_mm/deep_gemm.py
@@ -46,6 +46,13 @@
     @classmethod
     def is_supported(cls, compute_capability=None):
         if not current_platform.is_cuda():
             return False, "DeepGEMM is only supported on cuda platform"
+        # sm_120 (RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell) reports as Blackwell and imports
+        # DeepGEMM fine, but has no scale-factor layout for block-scaled FP8:
+        # transform_sf_into_required_layout asserts "Unknown SF transformation".
+        if current_platform.is_device_capability_family(120):
+            return False, (
+                "DeepGEMM has no sm_120 scale-factor layout for block-scaled FP8"
+            )
         if not is_deep_gemm_supported():
             return False, "Currently, only Hopper and Blackwell GPUs are supported."
         return True, None
